A||X||49||V8 Mikie||New V-8 kit Available in July||||4||
Z||000000||V8 Mikie||06-19-2000||10:27 PM||||If you are standing up, please sit down.  We have the most exciting news for Fiero enthusiasts since 1983.  Here at V8Mikie's, we have been surveying the market of V8 Kits for Fiero's for approx. 5 years now, and to put it lightly, we are NOT impressed.  Shoddy, weakly designed V8 Kits have been running rampant in the Fiero community like the Bubonic Plague, and that will stop shortly!  We have also been talking to dissatisfied customers (not hard to find) whom often mention the shaky Fiero axles and tranny.  So our mission was to develop a new V8 kit, cheap and reliable, with good customer service.  So V8Mikie's was born.  We use slightly modified Ford axles, and the Taurus SHO tranny to center the engine on the engine cradle. Since the SHO tranny is much thinner, There is no cutting holes in the Space frame whereby weaking the car.  We didn't take the easy way out on this kit, we did our homework and actually came up with a quality product.  This is just a sneak preview, we will provide all the intricate details in the debut of our website, <A HREF="http://www.v8mikie.com," TARGET=_blank>www.v8mikie.com,</A>  which is due up around mid-July.  This complete kit will be offered at an amazingly low price, with your choice of custom parts and different engine sizes including the New All aluminum LS-1 Engine.  When we say "complete" we mean COMPLETE! Engines and Transmissions can also be purchased through us. The kit comes with all parts needed and a 165 page HARDBACK manual to assist you in your swap.  This kit has been designed by professional engineers, 2 from GM and 1 From Ford, with a combined total of 30 YEARS experience.  Pictures and Bio's of all three genius' will be on the website.  Here at V8 Mikie, we have invested a lot of money and patient time, developing a quality product, not a slapped together peice of junk.  We have a better attitude, "Ugh, gee the water pump wont fit, screw it, cut a hole."  There is none of these mickey mouse botch jobs in this kit, 100% A-1.  Keep your eye out for the best V8 conversion kits available for the Pontiac Fiero, coming in July....<P><BR>-V8 Mikie, Inc<BR>Designers.....<BR>Mike McCallister - GM Design Engineer, 9 yrs.<BR>Tom Shulster - GM Design Engineer, 18 yrs.<BR>Suzanne Mathers - Ford SVT Design Team, 3 yrs.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-19-2000||10:42 PM||||OK, will still be here in July.<p>[This message has been edited by Phaeton (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||12
