Z||000012||mbramble||06-20-2000||07:13 AM||||Uhhhhh, I would have to say something is amiss here.  The first posting may have fooled me since I know nothing about cars.  However, the second one about the high cost of a domain name -- I don't think so.  I just checked and the domain v8mikie.com is available.  Unless you are trying to get a very famous/recognizable one that someone has 'squatted on' in hopes of making big money, the cost of a domain name at last check was $70 for two years, $35 per year after that.  That's high??!!  Wonder how much money went into R&D then!   I pay $20 per month for a web host that provides 100MB storage, database support, etc., etc., etc.,  You can get them much cheaper if you have lower requirements.  There are also plenty of places that provide free space if you care to put up with their advertising.<P>In my opionion, if this were serious, they would have at least already purchased the doamin name before they mentioned it in public, since I could go out and buy it right now if I cared to.<P>Results of a query to the InterNIC WHOIS database for v8mikie.com:<P>The domain "v8mikie.com" is available! You may register this domain. Visit our On-Line Order Form to purchase service using this domain name. <P><BR>Just my opinion!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||V8 Mikie||06-20-2000||09:56 AM||||Wow, you'd think designing a kit for 5 years to help the fiero community out would be enough, but then you have to cut down on my buisness techniques.  We're starting this project out Grassroots, to let the average fiero owner get a shot at an affordable v-8 kit. Most of my money is spent. I've been financing this project for 5 years now. After we get results and opinions on our kits, then we're going to get bigger, but we're not going to make the mistake of throwing what he have out into the big time and then getting hung by making one simple mistake.  These kit's do infact leave you with many options as far as which engine you desire to run, and believe it or not, it's actually easier to install a ford 5 liter, or a 351 windsor.  We've been running a stroked 351 windsor with a 96 Taurus SHO tranny with LSD, for over a year now with no major problems, this car is very quick.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||V8 Mikie||06-20-2000||09:57 AM||||Wow, you'd think designing a kit for 5 years to help the fiero community out would be enough, but then you have to cut down on my buisness techniques.  We're starting this project out Grassroots, to let the average fiero owner get a shot at an affordable v-8 kit. Most of my money is spent. I've been financing this project for 5 years now. After we get results and opinions on our kits, then we're going to get bigger, but we're not going to make the mistake of throwing what he have out into the big time and then getting hung by making one simple mistake.  These kit's do infact leave you with many options as far as which engine you desire to run, and believe it or not, it's actually easier to install a ford 5 liter, or a 351 windsor.  We've been running a stroked 351 windsor with a 96 Taurus SHO tranny with LSD, for over a year now with no major problems, this car is very quick.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||lennyb4||06-20-2000||10:17 AM||||Hey mikie... You have to understand the current situations that have been going on around here lately. The forum members above are NOT questioning you , your product, or your buisness practices. Its just that we  had an issue of sorts arise with a supplier (to remain un-named) of V-8 kits which did not turn out for the best. And then the next day "POOF" you show up. I will be the first to admit that its one hell of a coincedence. If ( i say if because i do not know you or your buisness, and because of what i stated above) you truely are manufacturing more affordable and user friendly kits of high quality, and they work out good then from a buisness stand point you couldnt have picked a better location to announce them. If you are on the up and up and when you do get your site running then you will see what i mean. So im just asking you that you try to be a little more understranding of the situation and why people (including myself) are sceptical. And by the way... welcome to the forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>lenny||||reg||6
Z||000016||Spyder||06-20-2000||10:29 AM|||| V8 Mikie <BR>Where are you located and where is your shop?||||reg||1
Z||000017||mrfixit58||06-20-2000||10:35 AM||||Yea Mikie, what LENNYB4 said.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>This group is always looking for a better, faster, and cheaper way to push these little cars around. A while back, someone from England joined and spoke of his VW powered 6-speed GT and, man, did the questions start flying. As far as I know, were still waiting on this guy to get back to us on his source for the transmission (it was modified from a 5-speed here in the states).<P>I welcome vendors and really appreciate your taking the time to let us in on your project on the "ground floor". The problem came in when your announcement didn't come with any proof like some basic pictures (hint, hint) and statements like "much cheaper" (numbers, please).<P>Personally, I'm excited about your contribution. I don't know much about the SHO tranny and you can be assured that I and a lot of other people on this list will have a LOT of questions (like did it come with a 5-speed?). I'm looking forward to learning more. <P>Welcome to the forum and, I hope, no hard feelings,<BR>Roy||||reg||14
