Z||000025||bHooper||06-20-2000||05:00 PM||||Normally, I stay away from contorversial issues, but I had to approach this one.<P>Hey Mikie, I do have a few questions and thoughts.  As I have obtained <B>all</B> of my mechanical knowledge in the past 4 months, I understand that R&D takes a lot of time and money.  But the business man in me (as well as the fiero crazy) makes me want to ask a few things.<P>1)It is true that many people start out with hobby's/personal interest and turn them into a business... if anything, just to help others that feel as themselves.  {b]FOR THAT, ALL 1148 OF US ARE EXTREMELY THANKFULL TO EVERYONE WHO DOES THIS![/B]<P>2)Having stated the above, it is human nature to get excited and jump the game a little.  I just hope this doesn't cost you in the long run (meaning: i hope that you are able to set up your net address and business operations as you have planned)<P>3)I have owned the same fiero for 11 years, and am interested in a engine swap.  Many of us are interested in actuall doing a swap, or at least understanding what it takes to do so.<P>4)As for the Forum... this is, without a doubt, a great bunch of people.  But just like anything else in the world; put 2 people together, you have a conversation; put 3 in the same room, and you have a debate; put 1000 people together and you have a hockey game!  No telling what could happen.<P>5)Yes, as several b4 me have mentioned, there has been a confrontation with another V8_-_-_- person.  Personally, I did not get involved in that.  Rest assured that did not involve more than a few of members.  Hence, the coincidence between your arrival, and the other's "departure".<P>6)As for domaine/internet registration... no it is not all that expensive.  Therefore, I would recomend registering your name and location as quickly as possible.  I will provide a link:   <A HREF="http://www.networksolutions.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.networksolutions.com</A> <BR>They are very trustworthy and used by most web hosting service's.<P>7)Pic's would be great!  If you don't have a camera... go to a kinko's or some other printing service.<P>I would like to say; thanks for joining our forum, and I do hope you are the real thing.  If youi are, you will enjoy this place as so many other vendor's have!<P>hoop||||reg||1
