Z||000044||mrfixit58||06-21-2000||08:07 AM||||Poor taste!<P>It's one thing to pull a practical joke on April fools day, its another thing to pull one just to try and goat a member into a verbal war. It doesn't matter to you that some on the list like and respect Archie. It doesn't matter to you that he has greatly enhanced the Fiero community by his effort to make a marketable product. The only thing that matters to you is that you get your jollies at the expense of others.<P>When you make a joke like this and direct it toward a specific individual, whether you mean to or not, you drag the Pennock forum reputation with you. Attacks, such as yours, return only profit for you and no one else. It reeks of eliteisness... like social snobbery.<P>So maybe you don't like another vender? Want to attack him? I remember attacks on other member/vendors that almost caused them to leave the forum. Their contribution of knowledge and products to the Forum and its members, now over 1000 members, was/is jeopardized just for the sake of one mans folly.<P>Personally, I think it's poor taste. What gives you the right to drag, or in this case, try to drag someone's reputation through the mud? Archie's weakness may be his short temper. You were hoping to take advantage of it. Suppose someone finds YOUR weakness and exposes it on the Forum? <P>Some will scoff at this note. Some may even try to poke fun at me and claim "poor sport" or some other drivel. But I will guess that, of the over 1000 members on the Forum, this will be a small percentage.<P>In the past, I've always tried to steer away for this kind of thing. No one should have to try and remind you that this is an open forum for sharing information. There is a good chance that Archie could have helped may people with his knowledge. But now, it's doubtful that he will ever post here again.<P>I appreciate people like TOM, Rodney Dickman, Randy Agee, Cliff Pennock, FieroShop, and others who regularly contribute to the continuance of the Fiero. I would hope that, in the future, you would think of how your comments affect those on the Forum. Not just the member to whom you've aimed the comment but all those who read them. You don’t have to agree with everything they say or like the price of their product. You can even make comments as to what you like or dislike. That’s what the Forum is for. It’s not for personal attacks for kicks.<P>Say good-by to Archie, thanks for making the decision for the entire Forum to alienate him. Who is next on your “hit list”?  Who ever you are, I hope you don't confess you real screen name. I would prefer not to know.<P>Poor taste, just poor taste,<BR>Roy<P>||||reg||13
